## Why This Is Asked
Assesses on-device CV design, latency budgeting, and robust 3D human pose estimation for safety-critical driving.

## Key Concepts
- On-device real-time inference with a lightweight backbone
- 2D-to-3D pose reconstruction and Kalman filtering
- Self-supervised pretraining from unlabeled video
- Robustness to occlusion and adverse weather
- Quantization and latency accounting

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for pipeline
class PedestrianPoseEstimator {
  constructor() { /* load detector, 3D head, PnP module, tracker */ }
  forward(frame) {
    const keypoints2D = this.detector.detect(frame)
    const pose3D = this.poseHead.estimate(keypoints2D)
    const pose6DoF = differentiablePnP(pose3D, this.cameraIntrinsics)
    return this.tracker.update(pose6DoF)
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to multi-pedestrian tracking with identity preservation?
- What failure modes are most critical in heavy rain and how would you mitigate them?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to design cross-modal, real-time computer vision pipelines that integrate on-device adaptation with differentiable geometry for robotic manipulation and planning in unstructured environments.

## Key Concepts

- Real-time monocular depth and surface normals estimation from a single RGB camera
- Differentiable probabilistic mesh prediction integrated with motion planning
- Few-shot (5-shot) on-device adaptation using synthetic pre-training followed by real-world fine-tuning
- Multi-task learning with shared encoders and task-specific heads

## Code Example

```javascript
// Core inference pipeline sketch
function forwardPass(frame) {
  const features = sharedEncoder(frame);
  const depth = depthHead(features);
  const normals = normalHead(features);
  const mesh = meshHead(features);
  return { depth, normals, mesh };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you quantify uncertainty in the mesh predictions to ensure safe manipulation?
- What strategies would you use to handle reflective or texture-less surfaces where depth estimation typically fails?
- How does the system handle dynamic scene changes between adaptation and deployment?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests few-shot, on-device adaptation, and robust pose estimation under occlusion and motion.

## Key Concepts
- Few-shot on-device adaptation; - monocular 6-DoF pose; - temporal consistency; - synthetic-to-real data.

## Code Example
```javascript
function weightedLoss(posePred, poseGT, maskPred, maskGT){
  const Lp = l2(posePred, poseGT);
  const Lm = crossEntropy(maskPred, maskGT);
  return Lp + Lm;
}
```

