## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical monocular depth reasoning and tracking in a simple inspection setting.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular depth proxy with known geometry
- Lightweight detectors, on-device adaptation
- Temporal tracking and data efficiency

## Code Example
```javascript
function projectTo3D(bbox, sheetDims, intrinsics) {
  // heuristic: depth proxy from vertical size and known sheet height
  const heightPx = bbox.height;
  const Z = (sheetDims.height * intrinsics.fy) / heightPx;
  return {X: 0, Y: 0, Z};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would occlusion or specular glare affect depth proxy? how to mitigate?
- How would you measure success and compare to a stereo baseline?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests end-to-end real-time monocular 3D pose with online calibration under non-ideal lighting and occlusions, plus efficient 3-shot adaptation.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular 3D pose under occlusion
- Online camera self-calibration
- Differentiable rendering with photometric losses
- Meta-learning for test-time adaptation
- Edge-GPU real-time constraints

## Code Example
```javascript
function forward(frame, state){
  const [detections, poses] = detector(frame);
  const extrinsics = state.update(detections, poses);
  const losses = photometricLoss(frame, detections, poses, extrinsics);
  return {losses, extrinsics};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle severe specular highlights? 
- How would you evaluate calibration drift over longer runs?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical monocular 6-DoF pose estimation in a realistic desktop scenario, with emphasis on on-device adaptation and strict latency constraints typical of edge AR devices.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular 6-DoF pose estimation from visual cues
- CAD-model-guided PnP integration for geometric refinement
- Synthetic+real data strategy with domain randomization
- On-device few-shot adaptation on constrained edge GPUs
- Real-time tracking under partial occlusion and clutter

## Code Example
```javascript
function computePose(keypoints, model3D) {
  const rotation = estimateRotationMatrix(keypoints, model3D);
  const translation = estimateTranslationVector(keypoints, model3D);
  return { rotation, translation };
}
```

